WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.212
The second set of risks is about
cost, capacity and features.

2
00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:09.964
Universal DDI licensing uses subscription
tokens that expire at the end of the term,

3
00:00:09.964 --> 00:00:14.975
so model total cost over three to five
years, including a hardware refresh.

4
00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:17.888
Size the reporting tier
for the retention you need,

5
00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:19.900
or make the SIEM the system of record.

6
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.917
Plan the hardware refresh around encrypted
DNS, put a stronger signing algorithm

7
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:29.787
in the build standard, and keep Grid Manager
runbooks for what the Portal can't do.

8
00:00:29.787 --> 00:00:33.763
Ignore stale collateral and cite
only the Marketplace record.

9
00:00:33.763 --> 00:00:36.909
Then turn the risks into
contract obligations:

10
00:00:36.909 --> 00:00:41.991
a certificate timeline with a remedy if
it slips, a BIND advisory commitment,

11
00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:45.910
the FedRAMP boundary diagram,
and a data export guarantee.
